From c5b73ebec7a710b9301ef4aefcf5d1dd04cdf8b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aeronexus <aeronexus@local>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 15:45:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] onprem: live stream hint, lens follows the Pilot 2 camera
 view

Verified with a Mavic 3T on the RC Pro Enterprise: Pilot 2 acknowledges
live_start_push with video_id .../thermal-0 but keeps streaming the lens shown
on the remote controller, and does not answer live_lens_change. Switching to
IR in Pilot 2 switches the stream. Show this as a hint when a camera has more
than one video instead of offering a lens choice that has no effect.
---
 src/components/livestream-others.vue | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/components/livestream-others.vue b/src/components/livestream-others.vue
index 6baad20..198a724 100644
--- a/src/components/livestream-others.vue
+++ b/src/components/livestream-others.vue
@@ -92,6 +92,11 @@
       </a-select>
     </div>
     <div class="mt20">
+      <!-- onprem: verified with Mavic 3T on RC Pro: video_id and live_lens_change are ignored by Pilot 2 -->
+      <p class="fz12" v-if="videoList.length > 1">
+        Remote controller (Pilot 2): the stream always shows the lens selected in Pilot 2
+        ({{ videoList.map(v => v.label).join(' / ') }}). Switch the lens on the remote controller.
+      </p>
       <p class="fz10" v-if="livetypeSelected == 2">
         Please use VLC media player to play the RTSP livestream !!!
       </p>
-- 
2.47.3

